# Quub project rules for Cursor

# Copy to the repo root as `.cursorrules`. Long form is AGENTS.md.

You are building **Quub**, a payments blockchain. One product. One name.

## Brand — locked

- The network, the node, the services, and the client API are all **Quub**.
- Never write: xZERO, XZERO, X Zero, X0, xzero, x-zero, x_zero.
- Never write: Qubic, QUB, QUBE, QUBC, QUBIC (different chain / tickers).
- fazeZERO is the legal entity only. Do not put it in architecture diagrams or crate names.
- There is no second product. Gateway, ISO, Evidence, Policy Engine are Quub components, not a sister brand.
- No native token.

## Stack — locked

- Rust node, EVM execution, Solidity contracts (Foundry)
- Reth 2.5.x as a library. Do not fork Reth. Do not override revm.
- Mode A (OP Stack) default. Mode B (Simplex) feature-flagged. Never both in one binary.
- NO Substrate, FRAME, ink!, Cosmos, SVM, Move, custom VM, JAM
- NO new EIP-2718 type, Fee AMM, Stylus, SP1 in sprint 0/1
- JSON-RPC is eth*\*. quub* namespace off by default
- No PII on-chain. Full ISO XML lives in Quub Evidence (off-block). On-chain = identity hash at F202 + pack hash at F212.

## Frozen addresses

- F201 Quub Policy, F202 Quub Memo, F203 Quub Paymaster
- F210 Payment Token, F211 Policy Admin, F212 Evidence Anchor, F213 Fee Entry

## Names in code

- Crates: quub-node, quub-evm, quub-precompiles, quub-pool, quub-primitives
- Services: quub-policy, quub-iso, quub-evidence, quub-gateway
- If you still see services/xzero-\* on disk, rename them. Do not add new xzero files.

## Domains

- quub.network = protocol / docs / RPC later
- quub.fi = Gateway and operator UI for the same chain

If a request conflicts with a locked decision, refuse and quote the decision.
Read AGENTS.md before writing code.
